WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
This broken bridge represents the central
crisis of moral logic,

2
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.840
the attempt to derive a moral mandate
strictly from factual premises.

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.500
The left cliff is the domain of what is
empirical data.

4
00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:17.440
The right cliff represents the target
domain of what ought to be,

5
00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.640
the required ethical conclusion.

6
00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.580
This gap is the Is-Ought Fallacy.

7
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.140
No amount of factual data, no matter how
precise or voluminous,

8
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.940
can successfully cross this gap to produce
an ethical conclusion.

9
00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:35.200
obligation. Completing this logical
structure requires a specific component.

10
00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.540
Every valid moral argument requires at
least one evaluative premise to provide

11
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.600
the structural link between empirical
facts and the final conclusion.

12
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:49.880
Without an evaluative premise, research
data remains morally inert and cannot

13
00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:51.100
dictate action.
